{"name":"Concord Grape","hex":"#855983","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"concord","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A state of agreement; harmony; union.","An agreement by stipulation; a compact; a covenant; a treaty or league."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A variety of sweet American grape, with large dark blue (almost black) grapes in compact clusters; a Concord grape."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concord"},{"term":"grape","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, round, smooth-skinned edible fruit, usually purple, red, or green, that grows in bunches on female vines of most species of genus Vitis and the self-fertile plants of species Vitis vinifera.","Any woody vine of genus Vitis that bears clusters of grapes; a grapevine."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing grapes or having a grape flavor.","Of a dark purplish red colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grape"}],"entries":[{"title":"Concord grape","blocks":[{"text":"The Concord grape is a cultivar derived from the grape species Vitis labrusca that is used mainly for manufacturing grape juice. It is a hybrid grape, crossed with one-third Vitis vinifera, and is named after Concord, Massachusetts where it was first cultivated."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/ConcordGrapes.jpg/330px-ConcordGrapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Concord_grape","wikidata":"Q393047"},{"title":"Grape","blocks":[{"text":"A grape is a fruit, botanically a berry, of the deciduous woody vines of the flowering plant genus Vitis. Grapes are a non-climacteric type of fruit, generally occurring in clusters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Grapes%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg/330px-Grapes%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","